# `project *, x = ...`: DS0117 pointing to `extend`; the columns after it are still parsed.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | project *, double = amount * 2
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..51
  PIPELINE@0..50
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    PROJECT_OP@20..50
      IDENT@20..27 "project"
      WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
      ERROR@28..30
        STAR@28..29 "*"
        COMMA@29..30 ","
      WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@31..50
        NAME@31..37
          IDENT@31..37 "double"
        WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
        EQ@38..39 "="
        WHITESPACE@39..40 " "
        BIN_EXPR@40..50
          NAME_REF@40..46
            IDENT@40..46 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@46..47 " "
          STAR@47..48 "*"
          WHITESPACE@48..49 " "
          LITERAL@49..50
            LONG@49..50 "2"
  WHITESPACE@50..51 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `project *` is SQL's `SELECT *`
  --> query:1:29
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | project *, double = amount * 2
  |                             ^ `project` lists the columns to keep
  |
  = help: to keep every column and add computed ones, use `extend`: `extend double = amount * 2`
